# Deploy after code changes

When you **modify** application source under `Kapil_pro` (anything that ships in the frontend or affects the billed Docker web image—including `src/`, Dockerfile, nginx config used by that image)—finish by **deploying** so https://kapil.cosearch.me reflects the changes:

```bash
APP_DIR=/home/ubuntu/Kapil_pro bash /home/ubuntu/Kapil_pro/scripts/deploy-low-ram.sh
```

Skip only if the change is purely local docs/scripts that do not alter the deployed web stack, or the user explicitly says not to deploy.

If the deploy step fails briefly with `curl`/`502`, wait a few seconds and re-verify the public URL—the container often restarts during the swap.
